  "description": {
    "text": "One card: _____'s Pikachu, drawn by Kagemaru Himeno and better known as Birthday Pikachu, which came with the All Card Calendar released on 5 November 1998 for the card game's second anniversary. The card says it may not be used at official tournaments, and Wizards of the Coast banned the English print, since any player could claim it was their birthday for the extra damage.\n\nDuring the Pokémon boom it became one of the most sought-after cards in the world, after Japanese and American dealers spread a rumour that its print run was tiny and had sold out within weeks; demand fell once the rumour was shown to be false. It later came out in English as a Wizards Black Star Promo and was reprinted for the 25th anniversary in Celebrations and Japan's Promo Card Pack 25th Anniversary Edition.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: _____'s Pikachu (All Card Calendar promo) (Wayback Machine copy, 19 November 2025)",
